## Summary
This article defends Nathan Cofnas, emphasizing the necessity of upholding academic freedom. It argues that harsh criticism should not be punished, even when it leads to tragic consequences.

## Key Points
- Defense of Nathan Cofnas for his critical perspectives in academia.
- The principle of academic freedom must be protected to foster open debate.
- Punishing individuals for harsh criticism is detrimental, regardless of outcomes.
- Advocacy for tolerance and resilience in scholarly critiques.


